        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ssrf): block loopback addresses for trusted hostname origins",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen resolving a host, if it matches one of the user-configured `allowedOrigins` (or `allowedHostnames`), the SSRF policy sets `skipPrivateNetworkChecks` to `true` to permit connection to local private network addresses.\n\nThis bypasses `assertAllowedResolvedAddressesOrThrow` in favor of `assertAllowedTrustedHostnameResolvedAddressesOrThrow`. However, the latter was only checking for link-local and cloud metadata IP addresses. It completely omitted checks for loopback addresses (`127.0.0.1`, `::1`).\n\nThis is a security vulnerability: if a trusted private hostname or local-origin resolves/rebinds to a loopback address, the gateway will connect to localhost services, exposing the machine to DNS rebinding attacks targeting loopback-only APIs.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd an explicit check for loopback IP addresses (`isLoopbackIpAddress`) inside `assertAllowedTrustedHostnameResolvedAddressesOrThrow` so they are blocked even for trusted origins.\n\n## Test plan\n\nAdded unit tests in `src/plugin-sdk/ssrf-policy.test.ts` verifying that:\n- Rebinding a trusted private origin to an IPv4 loopback address (`127.0.0.1`) is rejected.\n- Rebinding a trusted private origin to an IPv6 loopback address (`::1`) is rejected.\n\nAll 47 tests passed.\n\n\n## Evidence\n\nPassed tests on branch `fix/4.2-ssrf-trusted-hostname-loopback-check`:\n```\nRUN  v4.1.9 /home/dietpi/Developer/openclaw\n\n ✓ |plugin-sdk| src/plugin-sdk/ssrf-policy.test.ts (47 tests) 38ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  47 passed (47)\n   Start at  16:35:25\n   Duration  279ms (transform 100ms, setup 108ms, import 25ms, tests 38ms, environment 0ms)\n\n\n[test] starting test/vitest/vitest.plugin-sdk.config.ts\nThe `envFile` option is deprecated, please use `envDir: false` instead.\n[test] passed 1 Vitest shard in 4.43s\n```\n\n### Real Behavior Proof\nRunning SSRF checks with a mock DNS lookup:\n```\nstdout | blocks trusted private hostname rebinding to loopback\n=== Malicious Rebinding to Loopback ===\nStatus: Blocked successfully!\nError Message: Blocked: resolves to private/internal/special-use IP address\n======================================\n\nstdout | explicit localhost hostname still works\n=== Explicit Localhost Allowed ===\nResolved IP: 127.0.0.1\n==================================\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/4.2-ssrf-trusted-hostname-loopback-check",
